### HIGH: gemini (gemini-code-assist[bot])
**File**: `.agents/scripts/issue-sync-lib-ref.sh:496`
![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The `awk` script used for deduplicating task lines does not account for markdown code blocks (fences). If a matching task line exists inside a code block (e.g., as an example in a code block), it will be processed as a duplicate, which can lead to corruption of the code block or deletion of the actual task line outside of it.

Additionally, the metadata check for `pr:`, `verified:`, and `completed:` is grouped under a single `if` statement with alternation (`|`), meaning they do not accumulate score if multiple fields are present. Splitting them into separate checks ensures the richest canonical entry is preserved.

```shell
	if ! awk -v task_pattern="$task_id_ere" '
		BEGIN { pattern = "^[[:space:]]*- \\[.\\] " task_pattern " " }
		/^[[:space:]]*\\x60\\x60\\x60/ { f = !f; lines[NR] = $0; next }
		f { lines[NR] = $0; next }
		$0 ~ pattern {
			is_task[NR] = 1
			score = 0
			if ($0 ~ /^[[:space:]]*- \\[x\\] /) { score += 1000 }
			if ($0 ~ / -> \\[/) { score += 100 }
			if ($0 ~ / blocked-by:/) { score += 25 }
			if ($0 ~ / tier:/) { score += 25 }
			if ($0 ~ / logged:/) { score += 25 }
			if ($0 ~ / pr:#[0-9]+/) { score += 10 }
			if ($0 ~ / verified:[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}/) { score += 10 }
			if ($0 ~ / completed:[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}/) { score += 10 }
			if (best_line == 0 || score > best_score) {
				best_line = NR
				best_score = score
			}
		}
		{ lines[NR] = $0 }
```

