### HIGH: gemini (gemini-code-assist[bot])
**File**: `packages/gui-web/src/InventorySurfaces.tsx:612`
![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

Since `showPointedAppTooltip` is attached to the `onPointerMove` event of the entire `<section>`, it fires continuously as the pointer moves. Currently, it calls `setTooltip` with a newly created object on every event, even if the target element and tooltip content have not changed. This triggers redundant React re-renders and can degrade UI performance. Using the functional state updater to compare the new tooltip state with the previous state before updating will prevent unnecessary re-renders.

```
function showPointedAppTooltip(setTooltip: Dispatch<SetStateAction<AppTooltipState | null>>) {
  return (event: ReactPointerEvent<HTMLElement>) => {
    const target = tooltipTarget(event.target);
    if (target === null) {
      setTooltip(null);
      return;
    }
    const next = tooltipForElement(target);
    setTooltip((prev) => {
      if (next === null) return null;
      if (prev !== null && prev.text === next.text && prev.x === next.x && prev.y === next.y) {
        return prev;
      }
      return next;
    });
  };
}
```

